 ### [Ever Rendering](3814-ever-rendering.md)
-Ever Rendering is a real-time volumetric rendering method that uses 3D Gaussian ellipsoids as geometric primitives to represent a consistent 3D radiance field, avoiding the 2D billboard approximation inherent in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS). Unlike its sibling [Differentiable Ellipsoid Primitive](3490-differentiable-ellipsoid-primitive.md) which may rely on rasterization or different approximations, Ever Rendering replaces rasterization with ray tracing to capture volume density distributions for blending, enabling real-time performance without approximation errors in the transmittance calculation.
+Ever Rendering is a real-time volumetric rendering method that represents a radiance field as a set of constant-density volumetric ellipsoids, avoiding the 2D billboard approximation of 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS). Unlike its sibling [Differentiable Ellipsoid Primitive](3490-differentiable-ellipsoid-primitive.md), it replaces rasterization with ray tracing to capture volume density distributions for blending, enabling exact transmittance calculation without approximation errors.
 
