 ## Background
-VoGE (Volume Gaussian Ellipsoid) was proposed as a differentiable volume renderer that utilizes volumetric Gaussian reconstruction kernels as geometric primitives [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address the limitations of current state-of-the-art differentiable renderers that use rasterization and distance-based blending, which suffer from ambiguity when objects overlap [S1, unofficial]. The method builds on the power of volume rendering with high-quality occlusion reasoning shown by Mildenhall et al. (2020) and Schwarz et al. (2020), but adapts it to explicit Gaussian ellipsoids [S1, unofficial]. The code is available at https://github.com/Angtian/VoGE [S1, unofficial].
